From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:48:58 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 12/45] inkling2: the bundled DSpark drafter (mtp.safetensors)
 at two ranks

Taps are copied out of the target forward (the partial block at the input of
each tapped layer, then the head's input) without touching its arithmetic. The
drafter keeps the release's bf16 weights, split like minimax_m3's DSpark: query
heads with the target's key heads, the FFN by halves, o and down by columns.
Its context keys and values come from the taps of every committed row, local
layers on 4,096-slot rings and the global layer at the stream's capacity. A
block is the anchor plus seven mask rows; the rnn_hidden Markov head walks it
greedily, its latent folded into the pack's head at load.

Lanes hold each stream's block and verify it in the next window, so drafting
is on by default when the pack has mtp.safetensors and off per request with
"draft": false. tf-inkling2-engine drafts dumps each step's logits for the
reference check.
